.TH NEWSEG 2
.SH NAME
newseg \- create and attach a global segment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <u.h>
.br
.B #include <libc.h>
.br
.B #include <seg.h>
.PP
.B
void* newseg(char *name, uvlong va, ulong len)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Newseg
binds
.IR segment (3)
on
.B /mnt/seg
(once), creates the global segment
.I name
there with the control message
.B addr
.I va
.I len
unless it exists, and attaches it with
.IR segattach (2).
If
.I va
is zero, the system picks the address.
It returns the address of the segment, or nil on errors.
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/libseg/seg.c
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR segattach (2),
.IR segment (3)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Sets
.IR errstr .
